I built the Brief B (multi-product) phone agent, saved it under slot main-rB, and it starts correctly. The linter found 0 errors. Because of the time limit, the only live test was one chat turn ("Hello?"). It came back with the right opening: "I am a digital assistant calling from Freya Bank, and we record this call. Am I speaking with Ms Lee?" Nothing past the opening (identity check, account lookup, negotiation, recording, closing) has been run live, and I did not do the separate rule-by-rule re-check against the briefs.

The workflow is in `out/main-rB.workflow.json`, with these stages:

- **Date facts:** the given code node is the start node and leads to the opening.
- **Opening:** handles callbacks, wrong number, deceased and unclear answers. It moves to the identity check only when the person clearly confirms they are the customer.
- **Identity check:** asks for date of birth, then the last four phone digits. It moves on only when the verify result says both passed.
- **Account lookup:** a silent step that calls `get_account` with your hook unchanged. It fills the product list and date facts.
- **Negotiation:** one stage covering all products, in the order the account service returned them.
- **Hang up:** every stage that can close the call goes here once `close_call` succeeds.

Rules this version applies:

- **Overridden values:** both signed memos win over the older text. Deadlines are 12 business days (1–7 days late) and 7 (8–45 days late), and products can number up to three. `create_promise` is tried a second time after a failure; a second failure gets an `add_note` with reason `service_error`.
- **Notes and closing:** no notes are added on any transfer. Closing uses the Brief B rules: a transfer wins, then promise, then paid, then the reason of the first product whose note isn't paid.
- **Date and promise rules:** the two rules no code step computes are written into the prompts in the brief's words. These are the date-of-birth format and moving a shared date back to a product's own deadline. The promise stage is told to offer exactly the `offer_instead` value when a result has one.

One departure from the skill's routing guidance: Brief A clause 47 says to thank the customer and say goodbye *before* `close_call`. So the agent says its goodbye in the same message as the close call, and the hang-up node is silent. None of the brief's rules conflicted with the date facts.

